FerrionOS change to relibc (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 74b5e7e315043a21b599f271d5692727aa54f64d with the FerrionOS patches before it in recipe.toml applied, ferrion-gpu-blob.patch last among them. It carries the command submission, fence descriptor export and wait requests of slice GP4 (lane gp4-submit):
- redox-ioctl: adds VirtgpuWait payload for DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_WAIT (0x48), VirtgpuFenceState, fence dup commands and submission bounds constants, with a round-trip unit test.
- sys_ioctl/redox/drm.rs: forwards DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_EXECBUFFER (0x42) and DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_WAIT (0x48). Requires syncobj_stride == 16 only when a sync-object count is nonzero, bounds array counts and command size, and turns VIRTGPU_EXECBUF_FENCE_FD_OUT into a close-on-exec fence descriptor via dup on the render handle.

